        "id": "title",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "body": "# LongBench-v2: Hybrid, Iterative, and Direct Ablation"
      },
      {
        "id": "executive_summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## Executive Summary\n\n- **Hybrid improved full-run quality:** 737 correct answers (48.84%) versus 708 (46.92%), a gain of 29 answers and 1.92 percentage points.\n- **Hybrid finished 4.72× faster:** 2.03 hours versus 9.56 hours, saving 7.54 hours (78.82%).\n- **Hybrid used 118,507,121 fewer tokens:** 60,816,980 versus 179,324,101, a 66.09% reduction; API calls fell 86.47%.\n- **On the shared 503 originals, hybrid led the direct ablation by 16 answers:** 246/503 (48.91%) versus 230/503 (45.73%), a gain of 3.18 percentage points."
      },
      {
        "id": "headline_metrics",
        "type": "metric-strip",
        "layout": "full",
        "cardIds": ["accuracy_card", "runtime_card", "tokens_card", "input_savings_card", "calls_card", "direct_ablation_card"]
      },
      {
        "id": "topline_takeaway",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## Hybrid wins the end-to-end comparison\n\nBoth manifests cover the same 1,509 rows, model pair, suite hash, source hash, and cold-start condition. Hybrid is better on overall accuracy, runtime, API calls, and token volume; the exact totals are below."
      },
      {
        "id": "topline_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "topline_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "resource_takeaway",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## Resource use fell across every tracked measure\n\nHybrid reduced elapsed time by 78.82%, API calls by 86.47%, input tokens by 65.40%, output tokens by 99.81%, and total tokens by 66.09%. The chart shows the relative reductions; the tables retain exact counts and both manifest baselines."
      },
      {
        "id": "efficiency_chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "layout": "full",
        "chartId": "efficiency_reduction_chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "token_volume_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "token_volume_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "token_baseline_note",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "### Hybrid moved below both context baselines\n\nAgainst the shared 213,816,093-token full-context baseline, hybrid saved 153,006,055 input tokens (71.56%) versus 38,087,835 (17.81%) for iterative. Against the 71,272,031-token unique-source estimate, iterative used 104,456,227 extra tokens (shown as -146.56% savings), while hybrid saved 10,461,993 (14.68%)."
      },
      {
        "id": "token_baseline_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "token_baseline_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "quality_takeaway",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## Accuracy improved overall and for every row type\n\nHybrid gained 1.92 points overall, 1.99 points on original and exact rows, and 1.79 points on semantic rows. Original-row accuracy is the cleaner independent quality measure because exact and semantic rows reuse the source-group answer."
      },
      {
        "id": "quality_chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "layout": "full",
        "chartId": "quality_accuracy_chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "ablation_takeaway",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## Hybrid and iterative beat the direct baseline on shared originals\n\nThe uncached direct run answered 230/503 correctly (45.73%). Iterative reached 236/503 (46.92%), gaining 6 answers and 1.19 points; hybrid reached 246/503 (48.91%), gaining 16 answers and 3.18 points."
      },
      {
        "id": "ablation_chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "layout": "full",
        "chartId": "ablation_accuracy_chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "ablation_quality_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "ablation_quality_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "ablation_workload_note",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "### Full hybrid used nearly the same total tokens as the original-only direct run\n\nDirect used 60,010,270 tokens for 503 originals; full hybrid used 60,816,980 for 1,509 original, exact, and semantic rows—806,710 more tokens (+1.34%). Normalized per selected row, hybrid used 40,303 tokens versus direct's 119,305, a 66.22% reduction. Direct took 1.23 hours and 503 calls versus hybrid's 2.03 hours and 1,006 calls. Total workload and runtime are not like-for-like because the scopes differ."
      },
      {
        "id": "ablation_workload_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "ablation_workload_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "timing_takeaway",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## Search time drove most of the runtime improvement\n\nManifest row-wall time improved 4.74× and search time 4.32×; ingest improved 1.33×. Save and context-write overheads were essentially unchanged. Timing components may overlap, so they should not be summed into elapsed time."
      },
      {
        "id": "timing_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "timing_detail_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "hybrid_operations_takeaway",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## The hybrid manifest adds route and reliability detail\n\nHybrid recorded 513 answer calls and 493 semantic-verifier calls, exactly matching its 1,006 total API calls. It routed 406 rows as direct fit, 107 through dense-child packing, 503 to exact cache, and 493 to semantic cache; all 1,509 choices were valid with zero API or context-length errors."
      },
      {
        "id": "hybrid_operations_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "hybrid_operations_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "configuration_takeaway",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "manifest_comparison",
        "body": "## This is an architecture comparison, not a one-variable ablation\n\nThe data and model pair match, but search mode, chunk size and overlap, scan budget, prompt/decoder behavior, embedding contract, serving nodes, and run dates differ. The results support preferring the hybrid configuration as a package; they do not isolate one causal change."
      },
      {
        "id": "configuration_evidence",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "configuration_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "next_steps",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "body": "## Recommended next steps\n\n1. Use the hybrid run as the current full-suite candidate: it improves accuracy while sharply reducing runtime, calls, and tokens.\n2. Inspect the direct run's 107 truncated originals to separate retrieval benefits from truncation effects.\n3. Add route- and domain-level ablations next to explain where the 16-answer original-cohort gain comes from.\n4. Repeat the full-run comparison on comparable nodes if cluster-level latency variance matters for the decision."
      }
